{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RP-01 successful-retry usage approved without refinement. Maintainer response: “approve”. Decision: one successful outer Agent operation reports aggregate usage from every output attempt in its single in-memory result, telemetry projection, and durable JSONL row. Intentional delta: retrying outputs can increase visible `requests` and token counters versus the current accepted-attempt-only projection. Preserve one row per outer operation, use token fields for pricing, retain Pydantic `requests` as the operation request-budget counter, and include complete consumed-so-far usage in recovery and failure paths. Evidence: the probe observed current Rebar reporting requests=1/output_tokens=7 after attempts consuming 5 and 7 output tokens, while Pydantic whole-run usage reported requests=2/output_tokens=12; no repository consumer requires accepted-attempt-only semantics. Two RP-01 decisions remain: narrow exhaustion exception translation and additive logical candidate-call accounting."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786923781216513001,"uuid":"e5c0f68b-fe89-4cb4-91ab-38f64b446a83"}